  "lines": [
    "CDBG Grants",
    "CDBG program",
    "The Community Development Block Grant (CDBG) Program is a federal community development program administered by the Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD). The City of San Marcos is an entitlement jurisdiction, which means the city receives a CDBG grant annually to assist with housing and community development activities.",
    "CDBG funds are used to conduct activities that assist low- to moderate-income residents, households and communities. Activities must meet one of three National Objectives:",
    "Serve low-to moderate-income residents",
    "Eliminate or mitigate slums and blight",
    "Address an emergency need",
    "Program Year 2025–2026 CAPER",
    "The City of San Marcos has completed its Program Year 2025–2026 Consolidated Annual Performance and Evaluation Report (CAPER). The CAPER summarizes the City’s use of Community Development Block Grant (CDBG) funds and progress toward meeting housing and community development goals from July 1, 2025, through June 30, 2026.",
    "The final CAPER was submitted to the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) following a public review and comment period and public hearing.",
    "The Program Year 2025-2026 Final CAPER and prior CDBG planning and performance documents are available under the Reports tab.",
